{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And the hail shall not be anymore.</b> Meaning, it shall not be created anew, and what had already come into being and had come forth from the heavens — it exists no more. This is along the lines of what it says (Exodus 9:33): ״וּמָטָר לֹא נִתַּךְ אָרְצָה״ — and it remained suspended in the air until the time his word would come at the end of days, and it brought down the stones that had been upon a man (Berakhot 54a)." "<b>So that you shall know, etc.</b> Meaning, I am not praying on your behalf out of any belief in your words that you will send the people forth, but rather to show you that the earth belongs to HaShem."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:10.971478116Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}